>> title: Okonomiyaki
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: japanese, cabbage, pork, griddle
>> counters: Ramen Shop, Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: okonomi-yaki, Japanese savory pancake, Osaka-style okonomiyaki, cabbage pancake
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — it is turned once at five minutes a side: flipped early it falls apart, and one pressed down on the griddle goes dense
>> step.4: griddle in oiled 7-in mounds, pork on top, 5 min per side

Whisk @all-purpose flour{1%cup}(130 g), @dashi{3/4%cup}(180 mL), and @eggs{2%large}(100 g) into a batter.

Rest @&(~1)batter{} chilled ~{1%hr}.

Fold @shredded cabbage{6%cup}(450 g), @sliced scallions{3%stalks}(30 g), and @tenkasu{1/4%cup}(15 g; tempura crumbs) into @&(~1)batter{}.

Griddle @&(~1)batter{} in 7-in mounds in @vegetable oil{1%Tbsp}(15 mL), lay @sliced pork belly{6%oz}(170 g) on top, and cook ~{5%min} per side.

Finish @&(~1)okonomiyaki{} with @okonomiyaki sauce{3%Tbsp}(45 mL), @Japanese mayonnaise{2%Tbsp}(30 mL), @katsuobushi{2%Tbsp}(3 g; bonito flakes), and @aonori{1%tsp}(1 g; dried green seaweed).
